<title>USA: Nationwide to curb sales in coastal areas -- NYT.</title>
<headline>Nationwide to curb sales in coastal areas -- NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nationwide Insurance Co plans to announce Thursday that it will sharply curtail sales of new homeowner policies in coastal areas, the New York Times reported.</p>
<p>The move will virtually halt sales in Florida and also will affect areas along the hurricane-vulnerable Eastern Seaboard and Gulf of Mexico, from Maine to Texas, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Nationwide Insurance was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
